// spec: an object of a trivially copyable class passed through a C function's `...`, as MSVC passes one (C++ allows it): a class of 1, 2, 4 or 8 bytes by value, any other by the address of a copy; the C function's va_arg of the same struct reads it
// factorio: InputActionTestMaker's VariableToCode<QuickBarSetSlotParameters> and <QuickBarPickSlotParameters>, `ssprintf("...ItemStackIndex(%u))", param.targetQuickBarSlot)` with a 2-byte QuickBarSlotLocation, and PlatformBackdropCloud::parseCloudProjectionStyle's `ssprintf("\"%s\" is unknown ...", input)` with a std::string_view: wrong format arguments in the game (debug and error paths), which MSVC compiles
extern "C" import "c_class_through_varargs.h";
